<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds closed firmer but illiquid with prices effectively discounting a 25 basis point discount rate rise by the U.S. Federal Reserve on Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;We closed higher in line with most European markets but the market is cautious and empty of final investors because of the looming Federal Open Market Committee meeting,&quot; said one trader, refering to Tuesday's decision.</p>
<p>Traders said that a 25 basis point rise in the discount rate was already built into prices. The firmer escudo against the mark also gave a lift to bonds, they added.</p>
</text>
